AMX-FP8 dot products: exact accumulation, no DAZ on the FP8 inputs, NaN -> QNaN indefinite

ISE 319433-057 (the same since -055), TDP[B,H,BH,HB]F8PS:
- "For the inputs, DAZ==0 is assumed, for the output FTZ==1 is assumed.
  MXCSR is neither consulted nor updated."
- The pseudocode converts each FP8 element to fixed point, sums the four
  products of a 4-tuple and then all tuples over K exactly (int128),
  converts that once to FP32 (RNE) and adds it to srcdest (RNE, FTZ).
- "All operations treat the presence of an input NaN value (in src and
  srcdest) as resulting in an FP32 QNaN_Indefinite response", 0xFFC00000;
  inf * 0 and +inf + -inf are invalid, other infinities propagate.
The loop comment "FP32 MUL with DAZ=1" contradicts both the description and
the exact fixed-point computation beneath it.

The handlers instead widened FP8 to FP16 to FP32 under a DAZ=1 status and
rounded after every multiply and add, in two interleaved partial sums. So:
- BF8 denormals (which stay denormal in FP16) were flushed: tdpbf8ps of
  2^-16 * 1.0 gave 0 instead of 2^-16 (HF8 denormals widen to normal FP16
  and survived);
- cancellation lost small terms: 2^30 + 2^-10 - 2^30 gave 0 instead of
  2^-10, within a 4-tuple and across K alike;
- a NaN propagated with its payload (0x7FE00000, 0x7FC01234, ...) instead of
  0xFFC00000.

The four handlers now share amx_fp8_dot_product(): FP8 values decode to
integers in units of 2^-16 (BF8) or 2^-9 (HF8), products are summed in a
two's complement 128-bit accumulator built from two Bit64u (no __int128,
for MSVC), NaN / +inf / -inf are tracked per element, the sum is rounded
to FP32 once (RNE; its smallest nonzero value, 2^-32, is normal) and added
to srcdest with DAZ=0, FTZ=1, RNE.

Fixed in avx/amx.cc. Found 2026-09-29 while checking the FP8 instructions
against their specs; a randomized comparison against an exact reference of
the ISE pseudocode (6000 1x1xK tiles, K = 1..4, all four forms) went from
~950 mismatches per form to none.

